<DocsLayout title="Verification" description="Output verification, proof artifacts, security features, and hallucination detection.">
  <h1>Verification & Security</h1>
  <p>lean-ctx verifies AI agent outputs and provides cryptographic proof artifacts for every session.</p>

  <h2>Output Verification</h2>
  <p>Automatic checks on every tool response:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Path validation</strong> — Detects hallucinated file paths that don't exist</li>
    <li><strong>Import checks</strong> — Flags broken imports referencing non-existent modules</li>
    <li><strong>Secret detection</strong> — Warns if output contains potential secrets or credentials</li>
    <li><strong>Schema validation</strong> — Ensures tool parameters match expected types</li>
  </ul>
  <pre><code>ctx_verify()  # Run verification on current session output</code></pre>

  <h2>Proof Artifacts</h2>
  <p>Every session produces a proof artifact that records:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>All tool calls made (with timestamps)</li>
    <li>Files read and modified</li>
    <li>Compression ratios achieved</li>
    <li>Verification results</li>
  </ul>
  <pre><code>ctx_proof()  # Generate proof artifact for current session</code></pre>
  <p>Proof artifacts enable session replay and audit trails.</p>

  <h2>Security Layer</h2>
  <p>Active-by-default protections:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>PathJail sandbox</strong> — Restricts file access to project directory</li>
    <li><strong>Size caps</strong> — Prevents reading extremely large files that could fill context</li>
    <li><strong>TOCTOU mitigation</strong> — Time-of-check/time-of-use race condition prevention</li>
    <li><strong>Prompt injection hardening</strong> — Filters malicious content from file reads</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Zero Telemetry</h2>
  <p>lean-ctx sends nothing anywhere. No analytics, no crash reports, no usage data. Everything runs 100% locally. The binary makes zero network requests.</p>
</DocsLayout>
